m</span></button></button><button type="button" class="relative overflow-hidden cursor-pointer focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-inset focus-visible:ring-accent-100 flex-1" aria-label="View full image: Gta 5 Car Customization Online" style="border-radius: 16px;"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-bg-300 animate-pulse"></div><img alt="Gta 5 Car Customization Online" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-200 ease-out hover:scale-[1.02]" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="./car-builder_files/gta5lossantoscustomslivery_8be2408f-2e65-45d7-8bec-96cbd24405ea_l.jpg"><button type="button" class="absolute bottom-2 left-2 bg-bg-500 hover:bg-bg-200 rounded-full px-2 py-1 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-text-100 max-w-[75%] transition-colors cursor-pointer font-ui"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><img alt="" width="16" height="16" loading="lazy" class="transition duration-500 opacity-1 object-contain" src="./car-builder_files/favicons(2)" style="max-width: 16px; max-height: 16px;"></div><span class="text-xs truncate">animalia-life.club</span></button></button></div><div class="text-right font-ui" style="margin-top: -4px;"><a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13641943-visual-and-interactive-content" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-text-500" style="font-size: 12px;">Results from the web</a></div><div class="my-3"></div></div><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The page rendered as a React SPA so I couldn't pull the live content directly, but I have a clear picture of what you're building. Let me give you a thorough analysis and recommendations.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">🔍 Analysis &amp; Vision for the GTA Online Car Builder Visualizer</h2>
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">What You're Building</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">A <strong>vehicle customization preview tool</strong> — users pick from JSON-driven options (paint colors, wheel types, textures) and see a real-time visual result. Think Los Santos Custom meets a web configurator.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h3 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">Core UX/Visual Recommendations</h3>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>1. The Car Display — SVG or Canvas, Not a Photo</strong>
Since you can't use real GTA assets (licensing), an <strong>SVG side-profile car silhouette</strong> is the ideal approach:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Layers for body, windows, wheels, trim</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Each layer gets its color/texture applied dynamically</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Fully React-controllable, no 3rd party rendering engine needed</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">You can have multiple silhouette options per vehicle class (muscle, sports, lowrider, etc.)</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>2. Layout Pattern — Split Panel</strong></p>
<div class="relative group/copy bg-bg-000/50 border-0.5 border-border-400 rounded-lg"><div class="sticky opacity-0 group-hover/copy:opacity-100 top-2 py-2 h-12 w-0 float-right"><div class="absolute right-0 h-8 px-2 items-center inline-flex z-10"><button class="inline-flex
  items-center
  justify-center
  relative
  shrink-0
  can-focus
  select-none
  disabled:pointer-events-none
  disabled:opacity-50
  disabled:shadow-none
  disabled:drop-shadow-none border-transparent
