s="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">.</span><span class="token token property-access">isTexture</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240);">&amp;&amp;</span><span> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">(</span><span>
</span></span><span><span>  </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">&lt;</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(244, 123, 133);">div</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(244, 123, 133);"> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(240, 117, 128);">className</span><span class="token token attr-equals" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">=</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">"</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(155, 233, 99);">absolute top-1 right-1 w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-yellow-500 rounded-full</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">"</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(244, 123, 133);"> </span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">/&gt;</span><span>
</span></span><span><span></span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">)</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">}</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">It's a texture indicator — marking colors that have a physical texture pattern (carbon fibre, brushed metal, etc.) rather than a solid paint finish. Those are the ones that get the canvas composite treatment in the 3D render (pattern + color + crew RGB).</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">It's intentional and actually useful — it tells the user "this paint will show a texture on the car." But if you'd rather remove it or change it to something subtler, just delete those 3 lines from the color grid in <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">CarColorEditor.jsx</code>. Or you could swap the dot for a small <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">T</code> label or a different icon if you want it to be more obvious what it means.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
