          ease-[cubic-bezier(0.165,0.85,0.45,1)] h-8 w-8 rounded-md active:scale-95 group/btn _ghost_x02hl_49" type="button" data-testid="action-bar-copy" aria-label="Copy"><div class="relative text-text-500 group-hover/btn:text-text-100"><div class="transition-all opacity-100 scale-100" style="width: 20px; height: 20px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="transition-all opacity-100 scale-100" aria-hidden="true" style="flex-shrink: 0;"><path d="M12.5 3A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 14 4.5V6h1.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 17 7.5v8a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5h-8A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 6 15.5V14H4.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 3 12.5v-8A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4.5 3zm1.5 9.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5H7v1.5a.5.5 0 0 0 .5.5h8a.5.5 0 0 0 .5-.5v-8a.5.5 0 0 0-.5-.5H14zM4.5 4a.5.5 0 0 0-.5.5v8a.5.5 0 0 0 .5.5h8a.5.5 0 0 0 .5-.5v-8a.5.5 0 0 0-.5-.5z"></path></svg></div><div class="absolute top-0 left-0 transition-all opacity-0 scale-50" style="width: 20px; height: 20px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="absolute top-0 left-0 transition-all opacity-0 scale-50" aria-hidden="true" style="flex-shrink: 0;"><path d="M15.188 5.11a.5.5 0 0 1 .752.626l-.056.084-7.5 9a.5.5 0 0 1-.738.033l-3.5-3.5-.064-.078a.501.501 0 0 1 .693-.693l.078.064 3.113 3.113 7.15-8.58z"></path></svg></div></div></button></div><div class="flex items-center"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-test-render-count="2"><div class="group" style="height: auto; opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="contents"><div data-is-streaming="false" class="group relative relative pb-3" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Low poly is actually better for showing textures</strong> — counterintuitively. Here's why:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Why low poly wins for paint visualization:</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Larger, flatter polygon faces mean the texture tiles cleanly without getting broken up by dense geometry</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">The PBR shader does the visual heavy lifting — roughness, clearcoat, metalness, env reflections — none of that needs high poly</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">High poly models often have baked normal maps that fight your dynamic material system, making surfaces look "wrong" when you swap colors</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Smoother surfaces = cleaner chameleon gradients, cleaner matte reads, better chrome reflections</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>What to specifically look for on Sketchfab:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">For paint showcasing you want models where the body panels are the star — big clean surfaces.</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Topology</strong> — look for "hard surface", "game ready", or "low poly" tags. Target 5k–25k triangles total. Avoid photogrammetry scans (they're dense and noisy).</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Clean UVs</strong> — check the preview screenshots for any texture previews. If the UV layout looks like a patchwork of tiny islands the tiling textures won't sit right</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>No baked paint</strong> — avoid models where the paint color is baked into the albedo/diffuse texture. You want a model where the body is either flat grey or white so your materials take over completely. In the Sketchfab preview, a grey/white car body is a good sign</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Separate meshes</strong> — models where wheels, glass, and body are separate objects (not one merged mesh) give the slot system something to work with</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>GLB/GLTF format available</strong> — filter downloads to GLB directly, avoids conversion</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Best body styles per class for paint surface area:</strong></p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Muscle/Super/Sports → fastbacks and coupes, big unbroken hood and roof panels</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">SUV → boxy is good, flat door skins show matte/worn beautifully</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Sedan → long trunk lid is great for chameleon gradients</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Coupe → pillarless side glass exposes more body, cleaner profile</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Search terms that work well: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">"low poly car game ready"</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">"[make/model] PBR game asset"</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">"stylized car low poly"</code>. GTA V rips specifically tend to already be stripped of baked paint which makes them ideal.</p></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
