<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">That'll tell me exactly what we're working with. The issue is likely that Black Poly (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Metallic</code> type) and Black (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Util</code> type) have very similar hex values but the Metallic profile's luma-scaled envMap is still adding enough reflection to lift it above the Util black — which is the opposite of what should happen since Util is supposed to be glossy lacquer, not darker.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
