</span><span>
</span><span>---
</span><span>
</span><span>## Your Screenshot Script
</span><span>
</span><span><span>When you shoot in-game</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(211, 215, 222);">,</span><span> name files systematically so they auto-map to the JSON</span><span class="token token" style="color: rgb(234, 236, 240);">:</span><span>
</span></span><span>```
</span><span>/beff/images/
</span><span>  male/
</span><span>    jbib_0_0.jpg       ← slot_drawable_texture
</span><span>    jbib_0_1.jpg
</span><span>  female/
</span><span>    uppr_15_2.jpg
</span><span>  outfits/
</span><span>    cop_belt_female.jpg</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Then your component viewer can pull <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/beff/images/male/jbib_0_0.jpg</code> automatically from the drawable/texture values in the JSON — no manual linking.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Page Architecture</h2>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Three main views:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>1. Browse (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/beff</code>)</strong> — filterable grid by gender, category, tags, difficulty. Each card shows the preview image, name, component count, blacklist status.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>2. Detail (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/beff/[id]</code>)</strong> — full component table with drawable/texture numbers, step-by-step instructions, and a component image viewer where clicking a slot shows the in-game screenshot of that specific drawable/texture.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>3. Flip tool (<code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/beff/flip</code>)</strong> — user selects a slot + drawable + texture, see what it looks like, then get the BEFF combination that uses it. This is what makes your site more useful than max1382 — searchable by component rather than only by outfit name.</p>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What Makes Yours Better</h2>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The gap in existing sites is <strong>searchability by drawable/texture</strong>. Right now if you have drawable 47 texture 3 on JBIB, you can't easily find what BEFF it belongs to or what it looks like on its own. Your site can have:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">A <strong>component explorer</strong> — pick slot → pick drawable → see all textures, see which BEFFs use it</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Copy-paste ready values</strong> — click a component row and get <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">SetPedComponentVariation(ped, 4, 47, 3, 2)</code> instantly</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Gender swap notes</strong> — which female components map to which male drawable numbers (the gender swap list you already have on max1382's nav)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><strong>Conflict warnings</strong> — flag which component combinations overwrite each other</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h2 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Tech Stack Suggestion</h2>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Since you're already on React/Vite, the simplest approach:</p>
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">beff.json</code> — your master data file (same pattern as <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">vehicles.json</code>)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">useBeff.js</code> — filter/search hook</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2"><code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">BeffGrid.jsx</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">BeffCard.jsx</code>, <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">BeffDetail.jsx</code> — components</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Images served from <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/public/beff/</code> — static, no CDN needed at your scale</li>
</ul>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Want me to build out the data schema, the BeffGrid component, and the detail page in your site's style?</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="flex justify-start opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-within:opacity-100 transition" role="group" aria-label="Message actions"><div class="text-text-300"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><div class="w-fit" data-state="closed"><button class="inline-flex
