</span></span><span>│  [your og image]                │
</span><span>│  Car Builder — Stella Crew      │
</span><span>│  Visualize your GTA Online      │
</span><span>│  build in real-time 3D...       │
</span><span>│  stellacrewgaming.com           │
</span><span>└─────────────────────────────────┘</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Without OG tags Discord just shows the raw URL with no preview, or pulls a random image from the page. With them it shows exactly what you want — the image we just made, your title, your description.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Since this is your first time adding it, the simplest approach for a Vite React app is to just edit your <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">index.html</code> directly — no <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">react-helmet-async</code> needed unless you want different meta per page later. Just add these lines inside the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">&lt;head&gt;</code>:</p>
